{"title": "<span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical vs chemical properties</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质与化学性质</span>", "slides": [{"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties:title", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker\">🔥 <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Properties &amp; Changes</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">性质与变化</span></div><h2 class=\"s-title\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical vs chemical properties</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质与化学性质</span></h2><p class=\"s-hook\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">One bottle label says \"colourless liquid\" and also \"highly flammable\" — one line tells you what the liquid is like, the other tells you what it can turn into.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">同一个瓶子的标签上写着「无色液体」，又写着「高度易燃」——一句告诉你它长什么样，另一句告诉你它能变成什么。</span></span></p><div class=\"s-diff\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Difficulty</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">难度</span> <b>●○○</b></div><div class=\"s-meta\">⏱ 20 min · ★ <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">essential</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">必会</span></div>"}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties:keys", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker\">🔑 <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Must know</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">必须记住</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical vs chemical properties</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质与化学性质</span></div><ol class=\"s-list\"><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical property: observe or measure, substance unchanged (colour, density, mp, bp, hardness).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质：观察或测量，物质不变（颜色、密度、熔点、沸点、硬度）。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Chemical property: how it reacts to form a new substance (rusts, burns, reacts with acid, tarnishes).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">化学性质：能怎样反应生成新物质（生锈、燃烧、与酸反应、变暗）。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Matter has mass and takes up space; energy (heat, light) is not matter.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质有质量、占空间；能量（热、光）不是物质。</span></div></li></ol><div class=\"s-fig\"><div class=\"cmp\"><div class=\"cmp-col l\"><div class=\"cmp-h\"><span class=\"en\">Physical property</span><span class=\"zh\"> 物理性质</span></div><div class=\"cmp-i\"><span class=\"en\">🎨 colour</span><span class=\"zh\"> 颜色</span></div><div class=\"cmp-i\"><span class=\"en\">🌡️ melting point</span><span class=\"zh\"> 熔点</span></div><div class=\"cmp-i\"><span class=\"en\">⚖️ density</span><span class=\"zh\"> 密度</span></div></div><div class=\"cmp-vs\">vs</div><div class=\"cmp-col r\"><div class=\"cmp-h\"><span class=\"en\">Chemical property</span><span class=\"zh\"> 化学性质</span></div><div class=\"cmp-i\"><span class=\"en\">🔥 flammable</span><span class=\"zh\"> 易燃</span></div><div class=\"cmp-i\"><span class=\"en\">🟤 rusts</span><span class=\"zh\"> 会生锈</span></div><div class=\"cmp-i\"><span class=\"en\">🧪 reacts with acid</span><span class=\"zh\"> 与酸反应</span></div></div></div></div>"}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties:fig0", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker\">🖼️ <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Picture it</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">看图理解</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical vs chemical properties</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质与化学性质</span></div><div class=\"s-fig\"><div class=\"mtree\"><ul><li><span class=\"tn d0\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Properties of matter</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质的性质</span></span></span><ul><li><span class=\"tn d1\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical property</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质</span></span><span class=\"tn-note\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">observe or measure — no new substance</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">观察或测量——不生成新物质</span></span></span></span><ul><li><span class=\"tn d2\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">colour, lustre</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">颜色、光泽</span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"tn d2\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">density, hardness, viscosity</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">密度、硬度、黏度</span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"tn d2\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">melting point, boiling point</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">熔点、沸点</span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"tn d2\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">state at room temperature</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">室温下的状态</span></span></span></li></ul></li><li><span class=\"tn d1\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Chemical property</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">化学性质</span></span><span class=\"tn-note\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">how it reacts to form a new substance</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">能怎样反应、生成新物质</span></span></span></span><ul><li><span class=\"tn d2\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">ability to rust</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">会生锈</span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"tn d2\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">ability to burn (flammable)</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">能燃烧（易燃）</span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"tn d2\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">reacts with acid / water</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">与酸／水反应</span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"tn d2\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">tarnishes in air</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">在空气中变暗（失去光泽）</span></span></span></li></ul></li></ul></li></ul></div></div>"}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties:hard", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker hard\">🧗 <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The hard part</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">难点</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical vs chemical properties</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质与化学性质</span></div><h3 class=\"s-h\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A property is an ability, not an event</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">性质是能力，不是正在发生的事</span></span></h3><p class=\"s-why\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Students think a chemical property must be happening in front of them.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">学生以为化学性质必须正在眼前发生。</span></span></p><ol class=\"s-steps\"><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Ask: would testing this make a new substance?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">问：检测这个性质会生成新物质吗？</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Yes → chemical property, even if the sample is just sitting there.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">会 → 化学性质，哪怕样品现在只是放着。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">No → physical property.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">不会 → 物理性质。</span></div></li></ol><div class=\"s-try\"><b><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Try</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">试一试</span></b> <div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\"Sodium reacts violently with water.\" P or C?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">「钠遇水剧烈反应。」物理还是化学？</span></div><details><summary><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Answer</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">答案</span></summary><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Chemical property.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">化学性质。</span></div></details></div>"}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties:traps", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker trap\">⚠️ <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Traps &amp; tip</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">陷阱与提示</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical vs chemical properties</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质与化学性质</span></div><ul class=\"s-list traps\"><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\"Gasoline is flammable\" → physical (nothing is burning) ✗ → chemical (ability to burn) ✓</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">「汽油易燃」→ 物理（又没在烧）✗ → 化学（能燃烧的能力）✓</span></div></li></ul><div class=\"s-tip\">🎯 <div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Underline the verb in the statement — it usually gives the answer away.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">圈出句子里的动词——答案通常就藏在里面。</span></div></div>"}], "cards": [{"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.c0", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">What is matter?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">什么是物质？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Anything with mass that takes up space. Energy is not matter.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">有质量、占空间的一切东西。能量不是物质。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.c1", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical property — definition?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质的定义？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Can be observed or measured without changing the substance.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">不改变物质本身就能观察或测量到的性质。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.c2", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Chemical property — definition?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">化学性质的定义？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">How a substance can react to form a new substance.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质能怎样反应、生成新物质。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.c3", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\"Mercury is a liquid at room temperature\" — P or C?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">「汞在室温下是液体」——物理还是化学？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical (state at room temperature).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质（室温下的状态）。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.c4", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Signal words for a chemical property?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">化学性质的信号词？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">rusts, burns, flammable, reacts with, tarnishes.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">生锈、燃烧、易燃、与……反应、变暗（失去光泽）。</span></div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.p1", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Density, melting point and colour are examples of ______ properties.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">密度、熔点和颜色是______性质的例子。</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Do you need to make a new substance to measure density?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">测密度需要生成新物质吗？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">physical</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">None of them needs a new substance to form → physical.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">它们都不需要生成新物质 → 物理性质。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.p2", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which one is NOT matter?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">下面哪一个不是物质？</span></div>", "opts": ["<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">air in a balloon</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">气球里的空气</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">a drop of water</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">一滴水</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">the heat from a stove</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">炉子散发的热</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">a grain of salt</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">一粒盐</span></span>"], "a": 2, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Air is a gas — gases still have mass.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">空气是气体——气体也有质量。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">the heat from a stove</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">炉子散发的热</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Heat is energy: no mass, takes up no space → not matter. Air, water, salt all have mass.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">热是能量：没有质量、不占空间 → 不是物质。空气、水、盐都有质量。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.p3", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\"Diamond is extremely hard.\" Physical or chemical property?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">「钻石极其坚硬。」是物理性质还是化学性质？</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Hardness = resistance to scratching.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">硬度＝抵抗被划伤的能力。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">physical</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Testing hardness does not form a new substance → physical property.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">测硬度不生成新物质 → 物理性质。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.p4", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\"Baking soda fizzes and gives off a gas when vinegar is added.\" Physical or chemical property of baking soda?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">「在小苏打里加醋，会冒泡放出气体。」这是小苏打的物理性质还是化学性质？</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Is the gas a new substance?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">那种气体是新物质吗？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">chemical</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">化学性质</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Reacting with an acid to form a new gas → chemical property.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">与酸反应生成新气体 → 化学性质。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.p5", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which statement describes a chemical property?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">哪一句描述的是化学性质？</span></div>", "opts": ["<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Honey has a high viscosity.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">蜂蜜黏度高。</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Aluminum can be hammered into foil.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">铝能被锤成箔。</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Copper can be drawn into wire.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">铜能被拉成丝。</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Wood can burn in air.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">木头能在空气中燃烧。</span></span>"], "a": 3, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which one turns the material into ash and smoke?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">哪个会把材料变成灰和烟？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Wood can burn in air.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">木头能在空气中燃烧。</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Viscosity, malleability (foil), ductility (wire) are physical. Ability to burn → chemical.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">黏度、可锻性（压成箔）、延性（拉成丝）是物理性质。能燃烧 → 化学性质。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.p6", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\"Ice floats on water because it is less dense.\" Is this a physical or chemical property, and what is the property?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">「冰浮在水上，因为它密度比水小。」这是物理性质还是化学性质？具体是什么性质？</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which word in the sentence is a property from the list?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">句子里哪个词是清单上的性质？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical property — density.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质——密度。</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The property is density. Measuring it does not change <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">H</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord rlap\"><span class=\"inner\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"color:transparent;\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;color:transparent;\">X</span></span></span><span class=\"fix\"></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:-0.15em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">\u200b</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathrm\">O</span></span></span></span></span> into anything new → physical.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">性质是密度。测量它不会把 <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">H</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord rlap\"><span class=\"inner\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"color:transparent;\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;color:transparent;\">X</span></span></span><span class=\"fix\"></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:-0.15em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">\u200b</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathrm\">O</span></span></span></span></span> 变成别的东西 → 物理性质。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.p7", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Classify: \"Hydrogen peroxide slowly breaks down into water and oxygen when left in light.\"</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">分类：「过氧化氢放在光下会慢慢分解成水和氧气。」</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Are water and oxygen the same substance as hydrogen peroxide?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水和氧气跟过氧化氢是同一种物质吗？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">chemical property</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">化学性质</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Two new substances form, so this describes how it reacts → chemical property.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">生成了两种新物质，描述的是它如何反应 → 化学性质。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c4-phys-chem-properties.p8", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Two unlabelled clear liquids are on the lab bench. Suggest one physical property and one chemical property you could test to tell them apart, and say which test leaves the sample unchanged.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">实验台上有两瓶无标签的透明液体。各举一个可以用来区分它们的物理性质和化学性质，并说明哪种测试不会改变样品。</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Think of the ethanol example from class.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">想想课上乙醇的例子。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">e.g. physical: boiling point or density (sample unchanged); chemical: flammability (sample becomes new substances).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">例如物理：沸点或密度（样品不变）；化学：可燃性（样品变成新物质）。</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical property test: measure each boiling point or density. The liquid is still the same substance afterwards.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物理性质测试：测各自的沸点或密度，之后液体还是原来的物质。</span></div>", "whys": null}], "v": 1, "key": "topic-c4-phys-chem-properties"}